Praxyz reel B "A flight simulator for therapists" (26 s vertical reel): third-party and supplied material

MUSIC AND SOUND
A new original 128 bpm track composed for this reel, fully synthesized in sound.py (synth bass, FM plucks, pads,
noise-hat kit) plus a synthesized cockpit sound palette. No samples, no stock music. Not shared with reel A or the Eunoia reels.

FONTS (self-hosted in fonts/, SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/OFL-*.txt)
Space Grotesk: Florian Karsten, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/spacegrotesk
Inter: Rasmus Andersson, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/inter
DM Sans: Colophon Foundry / Indian Type Foundry, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/dmsans
JetBrains Mono: JetBrains, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/jetbrainsmono

VOICES
Narrator and the AI patient Rohan: supplied by the client (praxyz/voiceover-b/narrator.wav and patient.wav, generated by the
client with Sarvam bulbul:v3, voices "varun" and "aayan"). Used unchanged apart from filtering and light compression;
Rohan's track is band-limited with a short room so it plays "out of the app". No TTS was generated for this film.
Word timings: faster-whisper (MIT), model small.en, used only for alignment and checking.

PRAXYZ MATERIAL (the client's own)
Interface: redrawn in HTML/CSS from the client's React source (D:/EUNOIA/praxyz/praxyz-web) and landing copy
(D:/EUNOIA/praxyz/praxyz-landing). Patient portrait: praxyz-web/public/avatars (Rohan).
Icons: shapes after Lucide (ISC licence, https://lucide.dev), as used by the app.

FICTIONAL CONTENT
AI patients are fictional characters from the product. The trainee "Ishaan Rao", all scores, feedback text, rank (#12 · Skilled),
hours practised, the certificate and its ID are invented demo data, consistent with reel A. No real people, no testimonials.

TOOLS
Built with the Lemo-Opuscar film library (MIT; style: Dark Tech Keynote), Playwright/Chromium and ffmpeg.
